====Usage notes====
*The use of ''amount'' for countable things is often considered incorrect, with ''[[number]]'' or ''[[quantity]]'' being preferred in those contexts. Some go further by restricting ''amount'' to immeasurable things (that is, things that one cannot put a specific quantity to, such as intangibles), and using ''quantity'' for things that can be measured.<ref>{{cite-web|author=Amy Bryan|title=
Commonly Confused Words: Amount vs. Number vs. Quantity|titleurl=https://www.bkacontent.com/gs-commonly-confused-words-amount-number-and-quantity/|work=BKA|date=10 November 2021|accessdate=21 June 2023|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230621234329/https://www.bkacontent.com/gs-commonly-confused-words-amount-number-and-quantity/|archivedate=21 June 2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite-web|author=Craig Shrives|titleurl=https://www.grammar-monster.com/easily_confused/amount_quantity_and_number.htm|title=Amount Of, Quantity Of, and Number Of|work=Grammar Monster|accessdate=21 June 2023|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260217154505/https://www.grammar-monster.com/easily_confused/amount_quantity_and_number.htm|archivedate=17 February 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite-web|author=Manuel Rubina|titleurl=https://thetrcompany.com/en/the-difference-between-amount-quantity-and-number/|title=The Difference between Amount, Quantity, and Number|work=The TR Company|date=21 May 2018|accessdate=21 June 2023|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260221045545/https://thetrcompany.com/en/the-difference-between-amount-quantity-and-number/|archivedate=21 February 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite-web|titleurl=https://www.chegg.com/writing/guides/vocabulary/confusing-words/amount-vs-quantity-vs-number/|title=Amount vs. Quantity vs. Number|work=Chegg Writing|date=4 March 2021|accessdate=21 June 2023|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20241228084442/https://www.chegg.com/writing/guides/vocabulary/confusing-words/amount-vs-quantity-vs-number/|archivedate=28 December 2024}}</ref> However, when referring to something uncountable but measurable, the term ''amount'' is so widespread that it is generally considered interchangeable with ''quantity''.

